{"id": "ram-new-topic", "seconds": 1.406, "reply": {"type": "turn.result", "id": "ram-new-topic", "kind": "conversation", "operation": null, "intentOperations": [], "effectOperations": [], "question": "", "reply": "RAM is short for Random Access Memory — it's the temporary storage that your computer uses to quickly access and process data while running programs. Think of it like a workspace: when you're working on a document or playing a game, the data you're using is stored in RAM so your computer can access it fast. It's volatile, meaning it loses all data when the power is turned off.", "conversationKind": "knowledge", "preserveObjective": false, "responseLanguage": "en", "turn_attempts": 1}}
